# Shell scripts reach a Linux shell whatever machine the checkout is on: WSL builds the
# packages, and deploy.sh and verify.sh are piped into `sudo bash` on the target. bash reads
# a trailing CR as part of the token, so with the CRLF a Windows checkout gives them
# (`core.autocrlf=true`) `set -euo pipefail` aborts package.sh on its third line with
# "set: pipefail: invalid option name" and the release never starts. This is the one file
# that can promise otherwise, because it outranks the setting.
*.sh text eol=lf
